kind: vulnerability
title: "SimpleHelp OIDC authentication bypass CVE-2026-48558: exploited to plant TaskWeaver and Djinn Stealer, fixed in 5.5.16"
headline: "Exploited SimpleHelp OIDC flaw CVE-2026-48558 gives an unauthenticated attacker a technician session; fixed in 5.5.16"
summary: "SimpleHelp servers that accept OpenID Connect logins accept identity tokens without checking their signature, so a remote unauthenticated attacker can obtain a technician session (CVE-2026-48558, CVSS 3.1 10.0). It affects 5.5.15 and earlier on servers with an OIDC technician group and is fixed in 5.5.16 and 6.0 RC2. CISA listed it as exploited on 2026-06-29, and Blackpoint observed an intrusion that used a technician session to deploy the TaskWeaver loader and Djinn Stealer."
event_date: 2026-06-29
priority: notable
immediate_action: null
tags:
